These are very similar models, and along with the [[toh:plusnet:fast2704nv1|Plusnet FAST 2704N V1]] appear to be based around the same [[docs:techref:hardware:soc:soc.broadcom.bcm63xx|BCM6318]] reference design. This page covers just the specifics of the TP-LINK models; see the Plusnet page for details common to all three. The TP-Link TD-W8950 v1 model also has a very similar board and specifications, and the firmware listed below works on it.

TP-LINK calls these:
  * **W8960** (blue):  "300Mbps Wireless N     ADSL2+ Modem Router"
  * **W8968** (white): "300Mbps Wireless N USB ADSL2+ Modem Router"

  * **W8950**        : "150Mbps Wireless N     ADSL2+ Modem Router"

The main difference seems to be that the W8960 ships with no USB port and a lower voltage/wattage PSU, while the W8950 features a single antenna (150Mbps), no USB port, and a 9V power supply.

To make this easily found via search engines, the TD-W8960N may also be called just TD-W8960, and the TD-W8968N may also be called just TD-W8968. The 'N' may relate to regional firmware (WiFi regulatory) differences. There's no source that suggests the 'N' implies any hardware differences.

