==== Using CFE web (http) server ====
->[[docs:techref:bootloader:cfe#using_cfe_web_http_server|the generic CFE web server instructions]]


It's probably the most user friendly way of installing firmware. 

{{:media:doc:cfe63xx_web-upgrade.png|}}

The default IP address of CFE is 192.168.1.1. You should use a static IP in your PC since there isn't DHCP server available when running CFE.

For accessing this web interface:
  - Unplug the power source
  - <color crimson>Press</color> the **RESET** button at the router, don't release it yet!
  - Plug the power source
  - Wait some seconds
  - <color green>Release</color> the **RESET** button
  - Browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1%%''
  - Send the new firmware and wait some minutes until the firmware upgrade finish.

**Note:** trunk images have neither LuCI nor USB built in, you'll need to be comfortable with SSH (or [[#serial|serial]]) access and probably with [[docs:guide-user:additional-software:opkg|installing packages via the command line]] if you want those things.

